      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC we can only have 1 of those two present at a time.\n\nThe examples that I saw of using SkPngDecoder were like [this](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/tests/EncodeTest.cpp;l\u003d762;drc\u003d4a50bc3386e511462806d01f8e6f8be1aa0c1cb7) or [this](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/BUILD.gn;l\u003d1293;drc\u003df950263bb3d4b311e2cc12f0dceea24dcb9c2373) (in the build system).\n\nThe Rust version is coming ASAP after this (I just didn\u0027t want to entangle the two patches cause they didn\u0027t overlap), whereupon the `#define` parts can go away.",
      "parentUuid": "cb3bf6e6_2e2e441f",
